{"title":"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Case_1:_(meaning_)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Case 1:  (meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d0695ccf6813b231b54ca3ab86e93367c7a5f316.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; 1.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Case_2:_(meaning_)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Case 2:  (meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef3878ffaaf3c5c31e8dd0529c9eedd0874962e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\geq 1.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be nonnegative real numbers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/d/93d9379611a6571fd3dc7c634d9709adb841d1fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y + z = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" />. Show that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/4/e44d2934c954e2a90e79b042a59dca275fd6840e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq xy+yz+zx-2xyz \\leq \\frac{7}{27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"241\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that this inequality is symmetric with x,y and z.\n</p><p>To prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/7/817b092a4db75978fc56d08f7bdefd84fb67de60.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[xy+yz+zx-2xyz\\geq 0\\]\" width=\"195\" height=\"16\" /> note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/c/0fce09322356796e6adce205b1e7d6d0b7d7e5ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" /> implies that at most one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/a/c5af9f74a0405bc6a03c28c1027d600d2d8d1ea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\leq \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" />, WLOG. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/3/123707da60cd1acc74d0dd22999be61d0f2eb0c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy+yz+zx-2xyz=yz(1-2x)+xy+zx\\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"388\" height=\"18\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/8/71826702cbae8cb838c3d17c692f1324d2e40352.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1-2x)\\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />, implying all terms are positive.\n</p><p>To prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/5/4e50b390d60924994b6fb55b649bca59bf614969.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy+yz+zx-2xyz \\leq \\frac{7}{27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"208\" height=\"37\" />, suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/7/5c7993746c9a549d5e5d254717af503fca5fc447.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\leq y \\leq z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/c/e0ca25fb17db813630d00abd9527671280a99493.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\leq y \\leq \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"80\" height=\"37\" /> since at most one of x,y,z is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.  Suppose not all of them equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />-otherwise, we would be done. This implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/3/d23d9f484ba4a13a00bc54eb7be964d26320b0c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\leq \\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/5/a85b415718dc208e99af771d6ee576da8668d990.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z \\geq \\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" />. Thus, define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/0/cd05886b12da69917131b4af2302a667696d24c2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x&#39; =\\frac{1}{3}\\]\" width=\"50\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/4/b84e769b277b4a168488cb6df408c832d25fd937.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y&#39;=y\\]\" width=\"47\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daa9adad683889f484aaead68d3e6fbd11d3cdfa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z&#39;=x+y-\\frac{1}{3}\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/8/188d1a54a162fd5a8f695b33bbcc308013dea3d9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\epsilon = \\frac{1}{3}-x\\]\" width=\"76\" height=\"37\" /> Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/5/135443eeb93f2cfc2ed93777feca29d5c5a40684.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&#39;=x+\\epsilon$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/2/6a211d5c69a7b1d67fe057b0cf27e9635a8e50bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z&#39;=z-\\epsilon$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/3/503b92d5be1c85c047875f3b45b29bf2578e24d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&#39;+y&#39;+z&#39;=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"120\" height=\"17\" />. After some simplification, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/767ac5b793687b4181203e44ec8db94a173bf0c2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x&#39;y&#39;+y&#39;z&#39;+z&#39;x&#39;-2x&#39;y&#39;z&#39;=xy+yz+zx-2xyz+(1-2y)(z-x-\\epsilon)&gt;xy+yz+zx-2xyz\\]\" width=\"646\" height=\"18\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/f/6cfb90a04a3cedc01c2e460ffb70133ec66c9b92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-2y&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/1/241c8a927504fffbff2bf2a78f4de6dddd61d8b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z-x-\\epsilon=z-\\frac{1}{3}&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"173\" height=\"37\" />. If we repeat the process, defining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c5441118355611c1b907a7194f9eeb603a012736.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x&#39;&#39; =x&#39;=\\frac{1}{3}\\]\" width=\"93\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/a/c5a75448067e4c9c362d1cb6f0697b46ad9b22c5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y&#39;&#39;=\\frac{1}{3}\\]\" width=\"53\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48df0d5d942c6ad77c7911b4d6fbf3237e546524.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z&#39;&#39;=z&#39;+y&#39;-\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{1}{3}\\]\" width=\"163\" height=\"37\" /> after similar reasoning, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/e/1eefb0d900418ce5fedfbccaee2c59eba4aacee4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[xy+yz+zx-2xyz\\leq x&#39;y&#39;+y&#39;z&#39;+z&#39;x&#39;-2x&#39;y&#39;z&#39; \\leq x&#39;&#39;y&#39;&#39;+y&#39;&#39;z&#39;&#39;+z&#39;&#39;x&#39;&#39;-2x&#39;&#39;y&#39;&#39;z&#39;&#39;=\\frac{7}{27}\\]\" width=\"628\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the method of Lagrangian multipliers. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/421ff51cbbede858389a288305583902a29246f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x,y,z) = xy + yz + zx - 2xyz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"260\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/4/31435c325eb174654f396b930f935c00d901b508.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi(x,y,z) = x+y+z-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"201\" height=\"20\" />. We will find the local maxima/minima of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/4/11461f1cfeb75bbf63b77c040551d1f729b08970.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\{(x,y,z) \\in \\mathbb{R}^2 : 0 \\leq x,y,z \\leq 1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"286\" height=\"21\" /> subject to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/5/8f5799a5ace8666d73938f6e2d5bc994777a8f87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/9/ee934e54a88b75087b03641fdb6c4de702737fd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S&#39; = S \\cap \\{(x,y,z) \\in \\mathbb{R}^2 : \\phi(x,y,z) = 0\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"314\" height=\"21\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf344aa376979a8a81e8784f92fcb2381897ba65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S&#39;$\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is bounded and the intersection of two closed sets, hence compact. So every sequence in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf344aa376979a8a81e8784f92fcb2381897ba65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S&#39;$\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> has a convergent subsequence. Hence if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7c7138363d7b4c2ce11cf743289b0fa960e896.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_k)_k \\subset S&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" /> is such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/a/51a96e54c173c6d8d949c36df9f610296be2cd5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a_k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" /> converges to the infimum or supremum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf344aa376979a8a81e8784f92fcb2381897ba65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S&#39;$\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, there will be a convergent subsequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c332e4dd0f60bfa9528088d278b251da994212.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k_j} \\rightarrow a_\\infty \\in S&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"117\" height=\"22\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/c/32cc60ea209abb382d08c2957b574951d6951ab6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a_\\infty) = \\lim_{j \\rightarrow \\infty}f(a_{k_j})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"159\" height=\"30\" /> by the continuity of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />. Hence the infimum/supremum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf344aa376979a8a81e8784f92fcb2381897ba65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S&#39;$\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> will also be a local minima/maxima of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf344aa376979a8a81e8784f92fcb2381897ba65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S&#39;$\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>We must solve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/a/71af1061ae610add0f3b65f2143f66da74759365.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nabla f - \\lambda \\nabla \\phi = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />. This is equivalent to \n\\begin{align}\nx+y - 2xy &amp;= -2uv + 1/2 = \\lambda  \\\\\ny+z - 2yz &amp;= -2vw + 1/2 = \\lambda  \\\\\nz+x - 2zx &amp;= -2wu + 1/2 = \\lambda \n\\end{align}\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2a952eac27394f3cc59136e893ab52a38753d30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u = 1/2 - x, v = 1/2 - y, w = 1/2 - z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"302\" height=\"20\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/f/24f9ccc682d2ef02559c259133ff591c835048fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda = 1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/7/f07763d759dfb81a9e5c80dcfa1c889ea7770f67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$uv = vw = wu = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"150\" height=\"14\" />. WLOG <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/b/d3b23c4daa263a44c8d28489e214822ed44c9dc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u= 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/6/1a6e7891377451a4a8da65a9d1d3236ff728b267.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$vw = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" />. \nThen WLOG <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/f/c5f490387b7f39e9fa8152ae483296730a1ecc54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />. These imply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/f/19f596246ca26bf4619a29c03feaed8e58764f0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = y = 1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa9f0d97d2f39f78f05e05da40bf04f5a7c0726c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/7/a07fb197df7bb042844b9d1eac083956ce2cf577.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"17\" />. We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/d/11d7ecb46b55514bab8661fb218d60a72d70f95f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1/2,1/2,0) = 1/4 &lt; 7/27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"219\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/4/4142b1df8b62777d8f79957c86bdbcd3e97f2ce0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda \\neq 1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" /> then letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/d/7fda47727aaa21fa361d1a44b2908f12e1629e3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda&#39; = 1/4 - \\lambda/2 \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"153\" height=\"20\" /> one gets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/6/2f63505ef76782121105671f507612312a946e8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$uv = vw = wu = \\lambda&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"157\" height=\"16\" /> which imply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/6/2c609d986c9b6327f232a37817d837718e844df7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u=v=w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"10\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/0847bca76fbcc65f53f481b86842d1080903e5dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u,v,w \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" />. This implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/9/9a9b4b08e5174f1223bc933e5d3e40b1ab3a0630.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y=z=1/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/c/0fce09322356796e6adce205b1e7d6d0b7d7e5ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" />. And <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/1/121f5d360acdd80785cf79c8518a03a036079308.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1/3,1/3,1/3) = 7/27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"185\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Now to check the boundary of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/a/61a22c887ac5a83d3037cfed1cb322343469444a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq x,y,z \\leq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"17\" />. WLOG we must consider the cases <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/d/6bd3d68e77a39e1ea97e7009f70e12622fa76835.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/0/72079803c6fcdcfa95b6d7f383f6ad71f1eb631b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=0$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/d/6bd3d68e77a39e1ea97e7009f70e12622fa76835.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/c/08cc55a3a19c9f8cf005f17391db8ed355d2909c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/c/0fce09322356796e6adce205b1e7d6d0b7d7e5ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/6/7a618bda1847d33ede0ff905641965782665226a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x,y,z) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"20\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa9f0d97d2f39f78f05e05da40bf04f5a7c0726c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/0/b70ffce4cf1a0c80b224fec4a198b2cc55f46ddd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=1-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee2bd36606e8ae6c7d32c67babbacfaf1967a9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x,y,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" /> yields \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a43684cc5c0cf832265ebb6cab1f74fe705930a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x,1-x,0) = x(1-x) = -(1/2-x)^2+1/4.\\]\" width=\"364\" height=\"20\" />  \nwhich is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfbc430ce574ce8d64614536db8d173a44d53f00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/4&lt;7/27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/9/b7925d3f06ae9dc68ebbdce99b027979ed412ebe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq x \\leq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />. Considering all the values found we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/a/f7a17362fb006ec9676f98d41eaae25e5ff6ef78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq f(x,y,z) \\leq 7/27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>~not_detriti\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we prove the lower bound.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/e/caef33c163868776a5e10ac76785f462972b71a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"17\" />, then the expression becomes one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f79c3676b62fb47243e0d357c87115b6f3395e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d379b13c2338ee58a27252096b2544c9e8e37c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$yz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"11\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/d/2dd70347c7940f63ff9417e383548564fd92aff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"10\" />, which is clearly nonnegative since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/4/bb45f30e2008ddbaa076c6e64884634a49b16228.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y, z \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Now suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34e89b8bbfabfc5bde064524cf4c2a363b5b2a51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"17\" />. We need to prove\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/2/b02498d0642df430771eb49290265980add043a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2xyz\\leq xy+yz+xz.\\]\" width=\"168\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Dividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/7/d57d8fef9329fabd73078ae824a034e8a00e332f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"11\" />, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/9/6d9b4a13b96972ca025f307a4fe175221d380e72.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\leq \\frac1x+\\frac1y+\\frac1z.\\]\" width=\"122\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/c/0fce09322356796e6adce205b1e7d6d0b7d7e5ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" />, by the HM-AM Inequality (or Cauchy-Schwarz):\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/e/4cea83ca5114795d2edd7c1766e7f02ce40398e8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac1x+\\frac1y+\\frac1z \\geq \\frac{(1+1+1)^2}{x+y+z}=9.\\]\" width=\"242\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Therefore,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0c47720401dd89a63c500d8bd45bf0c8c96c5ac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 \\leq 9 \\leq \\frac1x+\\frac1y+\\frac1z,\\]\" width=\"155\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>and hence\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42ce777aa7719dc16adcd2714465ed7a3c5e75c3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[xy+yz+xz-2xyz\\geq0.\\]\" width=\"199\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Now we prove the upper bound.\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/c/0fce09322356796e6adce205b1e7d6d0b7d7e5ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore, we can rewrite the target expression using homogeneous scaling:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/e/96ebd2a62ca0a7677dbee9c768707d32c483696f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[xy+yz+xz-2xyz=(xy+yz+xz)(x+y+z)-2xyz.\\]\" width=\"456\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/6/776485b0a132cde44ffa957abbe39dd129d30a6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=3x$\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/f/67ff5d0cb9e6d3dffeac89c5af3558d5ae42e874.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/6/446bb681030165a855c43cbc054fca9610af1f5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=3z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/1/de12e8a2b7ad3124b609b10d033c65b8a479130f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" />, and:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/5/635680b6ec5f0efd7789aab367b37b0ba66b3bb1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[xy+yz+xz-2xyz=\\frac{3(ab+bc+ca)-2abc}{27}.\\]\" width=\"369\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Thus, it is enough to prove:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ff42dd2146deb2eca118e0ce7a2e7558eb12e88.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3(ab+bc+ca)-2abc\\leq7.\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/b/feba0f411ac2a519f7b144e7a68095a9c5737206.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=3-a-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" /> into the inequality yields:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/f/b7fdfc0f9d02f8a20cee599ed218aa0a1bd5ac8b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3(ab+bc+ca)-2abc = 3(ab+(a+b)(3-a-b))-2ab(3-a-b)\\]\" width=\"533\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/8/0886bb7061b0bf7a7380cde6f532ecc84dd1a19c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 3(3a+3b-a^2-b^2-ab)-6ab+2ab(a+b)\\]\" width=\"365\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/a/72a8e7096ac30f29a8c5c35d58d182cb741673c7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 9(a+b)-3(a+b)^2+ab(2a+2b-3).\\]\" width=\"320\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/c/05ce6b1b24021f7bac57083ccf3784d933cc20c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/d/29d5886e00dedd073f57500e340a0eec42783ed9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39a6740133910e6e86618ea6fceba885e9556e90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />. We now analyze the linear term in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef870ce9fefe09b80a97b05a7b9198414c1b35f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> by breaking it into two cases based on the sign of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/9/de92d2d89a9973f4a0997c69805d9db862fa17c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2x-3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" />:\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Case_1:_.28meaning_.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Case_1:_(meaning_)\">Case 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c54f3490228b2627c4293ef96b1e25ed560d6aa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x-3 &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" /> (meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d0695ccf6813b231b54ca3ab86e93367c7a5f316.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; 1.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Case 1:  (meaning )\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/3/273abd41b6d70c0e6b1ef1a9292005d6eaaf4e73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/8/4e8a2ae7b7cbf165999b3f6d11ddf1305413641f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2x-3) &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"20\" />, the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/c/51c140e98f9494310a797630fcd697cf032d8894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab(2x-3) \\leq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" />. Dropping this term maximizes the expression:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/7/fe7a7fc27e39275dc506f0e4c8c65f90b5fb7e7f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9x-3x^2+ab(2x-3) \\leq 9x-3x^2 = -3\\left(x-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2 + \\frac{27}{4}.\\]\" width=\"443\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>The maximum value achievable in this interval is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/beade0642f087924543b561ed9156a45d3617e32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{27}{4} = 6.75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"38\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302892992c37954251c2b4f4c0ebdcfd83630ae8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6.75 \\le 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"67\" height=\"16\" />, the upper bound holds true for this case.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Case_2:_.28meaning_.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Case_2:_(meaning_)\">Case 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/c/d9c15d742b7d048823f4b28fa004dfff93d682cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x-3 \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"86\" height=\"16\" /> (meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef3878ffaaf3c5c31e8dd0529c9eedd0874962e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\geq 1.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Case 2:  (meaning )\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/3/273abd41b6d70c0e6b1ef1a9292005d6eaaf4e73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f95e1714d92a190b8ebb75f67542ecc23593cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2x-3) \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"20\" />, maximizing the expression requires substituting the maximum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef870ce9fefe09b80a97b05a7b9198414c1b35f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />. By the AM-GM inequality:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/524016f79b61d38312ed42f4390562c07d8c5ef8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ab\\leq \\frac{(a+b)^2}{4} = \\frac{x^2}{4}.\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/4/fa4a480f5242d5984441a45159d9e60b2d1ae2bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab = \\frac{x^2}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"65\" height=\"41\" /> into our expression gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/0/530a8b0069b08cc91074557e3cf39caa681a2abf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9x-3x^2+(2x-3)\\frac{x^2}{4} = \\frac{1}{2}x^3 - \\frac{15}{4}x^2 + 9x.\\]\" width=\"340\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we want to show that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/4/bc4a7a2c41f251fb7b482ecbc12d8ca71fbd475f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}x^3 - \\frac{15}{4}x^2 + 9x - 7 \\leq 0.\\]\" width=\"201\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Multiplying by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gives the equivalent polynomial inequality:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/b/cabf293c193b7dcfd994fb9612130585ff5a6bd7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2x^3 - 15x^2 + 36x - 28 \\leq 0.\\]\" width=\"212\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Factoring this polynomial yields:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/5/c65ad797811e35132bc282d66842fedc6a9810a7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x-2)^2(2x-7) \\leq 0.\\]\" width=\"163\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/d/43d6a9e199dfd5a364e54c1ca96cfcdfa6af64fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.5 \\leq x \\leq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" /> (because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/d/b5d4291829b665d9d645e637005ce9a17baafd4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 3 - x \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"109\" height=\"16\" />), the squared term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/8/148ffbd025b7118e6aa32368542d68e288b0b542.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-2)^2 \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"21\" /> and the linear term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/b/fcb96ddcf10a70ea6ca0f66554c0fd2ef163f189.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2x-7) \\leq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore, the product is always less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Combining both cases, we obtain:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/f/8df7bd759e74738801effc5139d3cf45476fc16d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{0\\leq xy+yz+xz-2xyz\\leq\\frac7{27}}.\\]\" width=\"258\" height=\"48\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~ Ethanluyixuan2012\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/6pI2UoT8AqM\">https://youtu.be/6pI2UoT8AqM</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/U8R86eT_aUo\">https://youtu.be/U8R86eT_aUo</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO\" title=\"1984 IMO\">1984 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1984 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017174658\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.062 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.095 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 769/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 868/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 52/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 27591/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.485      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.485      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8081:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017174658 and revision id 289910. Rendering was triggered be